course: dictionary
lesson: 1343
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around a word, its context, tell you which meaning the writer wants. «A camper in Australia poured petrol on a slow campfire» tells you a camper is a person who stays at a camp, because a campfire is at a camp.
explain: Now look at «camper van». The word van tells you the camper is a vehicle. A camper van is a van with beds and a small kitchen, used for holidays. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the words around it?
explain: Some phrases use the word in a special way. «Happy campers» does not mean people who camp. It means people who are pleased. Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence and checking that it still makes sense.
fact: A camper is a person who stays at a camp, often in a tent, or goes camping.
fact: A camper can also be a van with beds and a small kitchen, used for holidays.
fact: Summer camp is a holiday for children in the USA and Canada.
fact: «Happy campers» means people who are pleased.
fact: One word can have more than one meaning, so always look at the words around it to decide which meaning is right.
exercise: «A camper in Australia poured petrol on a slow campfire.» What is a camper in this sentence? | A tent that folds up | A van with beds and a small kitchen | *A person who stays at a camp | A park ranger
exercise: «The camper van was parked by the lake for the holiday.» What is a camper van? | A tent for one person | A camp leader | *A van with beds and a small kitchen, used for holidays | A bus for school trips
exercise: Jo says, «We were happy campers after the swim.» What does happy campers mean? | Children who sleep in tents | *People who are pleased | Animals living near a camp | Campers who are tired and cold
test: Which two countries are named as places where summer camp is a holiday for children? | *USA and Canada | Canada and Australia | London and Wales | Australia and Scotland
test: «Campers in Canada left food in their tent; a bear came in the night to get it.» Why did the bear come? | To sing to the campers | To find a camper van | To guard the tent | *To get the food
exam: Aisha cooked her dinner in the camper, then went to bed. What does camper mean here? | A person who stays at a camp | A kind of tent | A park ranger | *A van with beds and a small kitchen
